Change(genesis='e30427e699992327267add669c3bc989f6d16525ba6f493121eec7778638e0ce', deps=('77cb289652b7bfb3b054aeeb04c4f9aa4927699c5659c956c4339c30192f417b',), event=Authored(todo='streamfirstcompile', at=datetime(2026, 11, 22, 17, 26, 36, 838600), actor='bmabsout', kind='suzateryTodo', created=datetime(2026, 11, 5, 0, 0, 0), body="The stream's first draw never holds the page's thread over 100 ms: the views module's functions are compiled before the first input, off the page's thread.", spec=Flat(value=0.62), rationale=('The owner finds loading fast enough now; the bar as written cannot be', 'met on a capped device by any design, so it is no longer a reason to', 'reorder other work.'), category='', waiting_on='', detail="In work on 2026-11-21: a session takes the cold first draw apart by the browser's trace and removes what holds the page's thread, in the runtime every page uses; the scene's bar stays 100 ms and is run ten times under load.\n\nState on 2026-11-22: a first change landed with release 2.1.208. The runtime reads the scroll box only for a step that keeps its place (a law holds that), and the zone's offsets are read by the warm-up worker while the module loads, where the device already remembers its zone: the first page's draw task fell from 45.6 ms to 11.6 ms on an idle machine, and the views' load from 501 to 452 ms cold and 273 to 219 ms warm. Not done: under load the stream as the first page still passes 100 ms in about one load in ten, and what remains in those tasks is the store's decode on the page's thread; the warm-up misses a few functions under load; and a warm visit's compiled module could be handed over from the worker.\n\nState on 2026-11-22, later: the design note docs/PAGETHREAD-PLAN-2026-11-22.md landed (release 2.1.215). Measured: the long tasks of the first page are the open chain's replica decoded on the page's thread and sent to the worker (each object is read six times before the core uses it), the box's fold cloned as objects, and the views' module's code cache; the views' steps are short. Chosen: the worker owns every replica and every answer crosses as bytes parsed once; the views stay on the page's thread; the views' module is compiled in the worker. Rejected by experiment: the pages' runtime in the worker (a keystroke's reply waits about a second behind the store's work). Five stages, each its own change, the first being the chains in the worker; it completes when stages 1 and 4 have landed and the bench shows no task over 100 ms.\n\nState on 2026-11-22, repriced: the bar 'never over 100 ms on a loaded phone' is restated. The note's own measure says that with the whole browser held to two thirds of a core no design meets it, and at ten times the store it needs a fifth stage in the views. What stands: on the fixture's store, idle, the first page has no long task of the application's own (met today at the median). Stages 3 to 5 of the note are not started unless a real device shows a delay a person notices; stage 1 is done for what it deletes and is its own task.", source=None, subtodos=(), notes=(), note=''))